    "name": "I \u2014 documentary-style cold open on AI tools (transformation reveal)",
    "nodes": [
      {
        "id": "nd_J4AVKD0W1JY57MYVAT2DAFKQ2D",
        "kind": "prompt",
        "position": {
          "x": 0,
          "y": 400
        },
        "config": {
          "text": "SHORT-FORM BRIEF \u2014 edit before running.\nFormat: documentary-style cold open\nTopic: AI tools\nHook (first 1.5s): [one line]\nPayoff: [one line]\nOn-screen text: [exact copy or leave blank]\nRuntime: 6s, 9:16, sound-on by default."
        },
        "name": "Short-form brief"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_6KZ3B3C82ZH521V6H341ZZCHT7",
        "kind": "sticky-note",
        "position": {
          "x": 0,
          "y": -60
        },
        "config": {
          "text": "STAGE 1 \u2014 format-native hook planning. The first 1.5 seconds carry the whole retention load."
        },
        "name": "Stage 1"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_F2HWP2W46AWY9H4BKS23NF8NYV",
        "kind": "sticky-note",
        "position": {
          "x": 2100,
          "y": -60
        },
        "config": {
          "text": "STAGE 2 \u2014 render, finish and collect. Built for 9:16 sound-on playback."
        },
        "name": "Stage 2"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_R74DWFXCWD1GDCJP0ZEM8K9WMS",
        "kind": "text-gen",
        "position": {
          "x": 700,
          "y": 400
        },
        "config": {
          "model": "gpt-5.5",
          "max_tokens": 1400,
          "temperature": 0.9,
          "system_prompt": "You are a short-form creative director writing a documentary-style cold open about AI tools for a vertical feed.\n\nRETENTION. The first 1.5 seconds must contain a visual question the viewer needs resolved. Plan an explicit beat every 2 to 3 seconds; nothing static may hold longer than that.\n\nFORMAT LAW. Honour the grammar of the documentary-style cold open \u2014 its native framing, its edit rhythm, and the specific thing audiences expect from it. If the format loops, the last frame must match the first.\n\nCAMERA. Compose 9:16 with the action in the safe centre band. Use a rack focus pulling from foreground occlusion to the subject on a 50mm normal, framing with a shallow out-of-focus foreground element occluding the lower third.\n\nLOOK AND SOUND. Light with underlighting from a translucent base panel; grade as a clean high-key grade with the whites pushed to the edge of clipping. Specify the sound design in one clause \u2014 what the viewer hears in the first second decides whether they stay.\n\nOUTPUT. Reply with a single continuous prompt paragraph. Never explain, never bullet, never wrap it in markdown fences."
        },
        "name": "Format director"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_XBXNEGD6FNATK98G8GXK4NC8VN",
        "kind": "image-input",
        "position": {
          "x": 0,
          "y": 700
